// tgvanity — vanity addresses for Telegram Gram Wallet (WalletTg), "12 + 12 words" format.
//
// Gram Wallet / MyTonWallet import 24 words as two BIP39 phrases of 12 words:
//   words 1-12  (anchor)  -> BIP39 seed -> SLIP-10 m/44'/607'/0' -> key that defines the ADDRESS
//   words 13-24 (signing) -> the same derivation -> key that signs; it must be set in the contract
// This program finds the ANCHOR (12 words) whose WalletTg address matches a pattern.
// The signing half is generated later on your own computer (finalize.mjs), which also deploys the
// wallet and switches it to the signing key. After that the anchor words cannot sign anything.
//
// GPU (CUDA): random entropy (ChaCha20) -> BIP39 checksum -> PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA512 x2048 -> SLIP-10.
// CPU threads: Ed25519 public key -> WalletTg address -> pattern. Matches are re-derived with
// OpenSSL (independent code) before they are printed.
//
// Build (GPU): nvcc -O3 -std=c++17 -arch=native -o tgvanity vanity.cu -lcrypto -lpthread
// Build (CPU): g++ -O3 -march=native -std=c++17 -x c++ -o tgvanity vanity.cu -lcrypto -lpthread

